"The Primary is a powerful Artonan wizard known by his title; he is Stuart's father."
"He has long straight pale purple, nearly white hair, pink eyes and calloused hands."
"He wears no tablet, lens or iris rings, has multiple spouses and rarely socializes."
"He reads a leather-bound book at parties."
"At the LeafSong gala he measured Alden Thorn by holding his hands and questioning him."
"His magic is a cocoon far larger than Alden's, one that could erase him."
"He says he doesn't hurt people and calls Joe Ro-den."
"He told Alden he is too whole for the two of them to avoid one another in the long run."
"Joe seems afraid of him and says he will make Alden's life miserable once he learns Alden's skill."
"His sister, pregnant with babies, arranged his meeting with Alden."
"Primary is the highest knight title; there is only one, the most powerful wizard."
"Alden thinks of the role as a cross between a nuclear warhead and the Pope."
"A telescope image showed him nearly halving a demon a tenth the size of Moon Thegund."
"He releases knights who choose their rest with an instant skill that leaves no mark."
"He released his own daughter, Sina-art'h, at about eighteen or nineteen."
"He speaks to Contracts directly and has little tolerance for petty restrictions."
"He sees Alden as future chaos-field support staff and means to reassess him near thirty."
"He and Alis-art'h are two of a set of triplets; their third is no longer with them."
"His name is Jeneth-art'h; with Alis and Tesen he founded the art'h siblinghold."
"His first skill, Cleaver of Strength, turns an enemy's greatest strength into a crack."
"He has six spouses, all former votaries; Olorn and Veln were his first contract."
"On a chaos-snared world he fought beside the knight Iella-inwer; Stuart was conceived there."
"Years later he struck Iella down with his skill to free young Stuart's mind."
"He is resuming a campaign to reopen a way to a place long abandoned to chaos."
"His spouses include Olorn, Veln and Calassa, and Stu is called his favorite child."
"He could destroy human civilization on Earth, though he would need help to find and reach it."
"He dipped bread in ceremonial wevvi to make young Stu laugh."
"He told Stu to act with full strength on confidence in his path, and made him promise."
